Special Agent Matthew Oliver:

On March 3, 2026, I wrote 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/record/oprd/01KJT9T6V8Q8PATA3JMZ8DD1ZW/> 
Deputy Director J.R. Collier of Oregon Parks and Recreation Department. 
I told him I was volunteering for the US Forest Service and working two 
jobs. I told him I intended to secure the funds needed to sue his 
institution for barring me from participating in civic government. I 
told him there was still time. It was the last door I was holding open 
for the man and I told him as much. I ended with refusal: "You will not 
bury this."

That same day, a man I have never met or corresponded with, using a 
title meant to carry the entire act, Oregon State Parks' Emergency 
Manager Jamen Lee, copying Deputy Director J.R. Collier, wrote 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/records/osp/attachments/01m1m4wf78xjpejj48d1jz4sj8-Electronic-Communications-Electronic-Communications.pdf#page=2> 
to the press captain at Oregon State Police. He did not allege a crime 
or threat. He sent the other man a link to my archive and invoked his 
Director and our Governor as shield and justification.

 From that moment on, I became a target of the state's police power, 
ultimately leading to the deeply unethical act of March 24, 2026, but it 
is not that act I write to you about today. No, today I write to you as 
one man does to another.

They started planning this in early March and brought you in only at the 
end, and you enthusiastically went along with their plans, participated 
when you called me to deliver their message (it was received in my body 
for months), then went a step further when you sent my information to 
the county deputy I share a space with. I lack the vocabulary to 
categorize that last act.

I am a United States citizen. That alone afforded me the right not to be 
intimidated at my home and workplace over my public speech. That it was 
done on the anniversary that same speech was punished by an act of 
displacement is a further harm by men who knew that's what they were doing.

And still it is not the worst harm in this record, because they did not 
have the standing with me to produce it. I am a United States Forest 
Service volunteer. We carry the same sigil on our chests, and you used 
yours to harm mine. I say this because it needs to be said, and with the 
hope you are the kind of man who will reflect when something is named to 
him. What you did betrayed something sacred. I will not supply the name 
of it here.

Their entire goal was to displace me a second time. And you helped them 
attempt it. I do not want that fact lost on the record so I am supplying 
it myself, right now.

I recently published a feature called Key Individuals 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/key-individuals/> to the archive. It 
lists three categories of dozens of individuals and offices, including 
one about you 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/key-individuals/#forest-service-agent>. 
I redacted the original park staff, the program manager who spent a year 
writing the disparaging account of me, and the records staff of various 
agencies. It is my considered point of view that no one who exercises 
force or holds responsibility for that use of force should ever be 
concealed from public examination. However, I have independently reached 
the decision to redact your name. You will be referred to only as USFS 
Special Agent wherever practicable. I did not do this for you. I did it 
because no one should face a permanent accounting of their worst 
behavior and our District Ranger made it possible for me to choose that 
outcome.

This email was written by a human hand as he hiked 
<https://rswfire.com/trace/01M55ECYC283C9NZH02RAD1X0H> from Tahkenitch 
to Threemile Lake all the way south to Sparrow Park Road. Then back via 
the beach next to the Oregon Dunes on a clear and sunny late October 
afternoon. He was still caretaker of the Siltcoos corridor as he wrote 
it. He had not taken that for granted once since men came to his door to 
scare him. No AI was used in the writing.

I require no response from you.

Respectfully,

*Robert Samuel White*
